P1 has no overall deadline: its 120-second timeout applies to each `exec`, while venv creation and file copies are unbounded. `should_stop` also excludes P1 time from its task-duration estimate. Separately, I reproduced `all_le_30s=True` with a missing P1 record.

The ZIP hash and contents match. The full test run is blocked by the read-only sandbox’s lack of a writable temporary directory; three probe tests and two gate tests using in-memory journals pass.
